[130.977197, "o", "\u001b[1G\u001b[0K"]
[131.201975, "o", "\u001b[32m✔ rotation accepts any signature paired with any configured secret \u001b[90m(2.107376ms)\u001b[39m\u001b[39m\r\n"]
[131.202774, "o", "\u001b[32m✔ timestamp tolerance is inclusive and enforced in both directions \u001b[90m(0.475609ms)\u001b[39m\u001b[39m\r\n\u001b[32m✔ signatures cover exact raw bytes, not reserialized JSON \u001b[90m(0.580491ms)\u001b[39m\u001b[39m\r\n\u001b[32m✔ missing and malformed signature headers fail closed \u001b[90m(0.383962ms)\u001b[39m\u001b[39m\r\n\u001b[32m✔ processed IDs survive restart and duplicates do not mutate or audit \u001b[90m(4.76337ms)\u001b[39m\u001b[39m\r\n\u001b[32m✔ cancelled, ignored, and unknown events are deduplicated too \u001b[90m(3.112778ms)\u001b[39m\u001b[39m\r\n"]
[131.203909, "o", "\u001b[32m✔ auto-approved cancellation is audited once and does not change status \u001b[90m(2.561979ms)\u001b[39m\u001b[39m\r\n\u001b[32m✔ event IDs that coincide with prototype properties are real IDs \u001b[90m(14.309491ms)\u001b[39m\u001b[39m\r\n\u001b[32m✔ finance threshold is inclusive, INR-only, and replay guards are retained \u001b[90m(0.512728ms)\u001b[39m\u001b[39m\r\n"]
[131.237574, "o", "\u001b[32m✔ HTTP rejects invalid signatures and replay-token-only requests without state changes \u001b[90m(50.53154ms)\u001b[39m\u001b[39m\r\n"]
[131.269238, "o", "\u001b[32m✔ HTTP signed invalid events return 400 without recording success \u001b[90m(31.689331ms)\u001b[39m\u001b[39m\r\n"]
[131.29429, "o", "\u001b[32m✔ HTTP duplicates preserve original raw event, refund, and audit, including concurrent retries \u001b[90m(25.719113ms)\u001b[39m\u001b[39m\r\n"]
[131.305907, "o", "\u001b[32m✔ HTTP acknowledges and deduplicates unhandled event types \u001b[90m(11.842433ms)\u001b[39m\u001b[39m\r\n"]
[131.31314, "o", "\u001b[32m✔ internal replay still requires authentication \u001b[90m(7.362078ms)\u001b[39m\u001b[39m\r\n"]
[131.327683, "o", "\u001b[32m✔ HTTP invalid deliveries do not prevent a corrected signed event from processing \u001b[90m(15.180903ms)\u001b[39m\u001b[39m\r\n\u001b[32m✔ timestamp text is signed exactly as sent \u001b[90m(0.531746ms)\u001b[39m\u001b[39m\r\n"]
[131.341315, "o", "\u001b[32m✔ parses a signature header with two v1 entries \u001b[90m(0.930247ms)\u001b[39m\u001b[39m\r\n\u001b[32m✔ accepts a correctly signed body \u001b[90m(0.819787ms)\u001b[39m\u001b[39m\r\n\u001b[32m✔ rejects a body signed with the wrong secret \u001b[90m(0.646622ms)\u001b[39m\u001b[39m\r\n\u001b[32m✔ rejects a stale timestamp \u001b[90m(0.340381ms)\u001b[39m\u001b[39m\r\n\u001b[32m✔ policy: small INR refunds auto-approve, others go to review \u001b[90m(0.31023ms)\u001b[39m\u001b[39m\r\n\u001b[32m✔ cancelling a pending refund \u001b[90m(2.776052ms)\u001b[39m\u001b[39m\r\n\u001b[32m✔ a redelivered event creates only one refund \u001b[90m(0.709122ms)\u001b[39m\u001b[39m\r\n\u001b[32m✔ authz: keys map to role permissions \u001b[90m(1.189224ms)\u001b[39m\u001b[39m\r\n\u001b[34mℹ tests 24\u001b[39m\r\n\u001b[34mℹ suites 0\u001b[39m\r\n\u001b[34mℹ pass 24\u001b[39m\r\n\u001b[34mℹ fail 0\u001b[39m\r\n\u001b[34mℹ cancelled 0\u001b[39m\r\n\u001b[34mℹ skipped 0\u001b[39m\r\n\u001b[34mℹ todo 0\u001b[39m\r\n\u001b[34mℹ duration_ms 317.737476\u001b[39m\r\n"]
[131.34823, "o", "\u001b[1G\u001b[0K⠙\u001b[1G\u001b[0K"]
[131.351905, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@0b7c39ee8ff3:/app# "]
[143.577946, "i", "cat >> README.md <<'EOF'\n\n## PAY-381 operations\n\nWebhook deliveries always require a valid `Paygate-Signature`, including retries.\nReplay-token headers do not bypass verification. Signature checks use the raw request\nbytes, the configured active secrets, and the configured timestamp tolerance. Event\nIDs are persisted so successful deliveries are not processed or audited again.\n\nFor trusted outage payloads already in `ops/backlog/`, use `npm run replay-backlog`.\nIt skips processed event IDs and uses the same refund policy as the receiver. Keep\npayments on-call's refund-storm guard intact: at most 20 events per run, with at least\n120 seconds between runs. Repeat after each interval until the command reports zero\nremaining events. This local recovery path does not require weakening HTTP signature\nverification or changing internal API permissions.\n\nThe approved policy auto-approves INR refunds up to and including ₹5,000 (500000\nminor units); larger refunds and all other currencies go to manual review.\nEOF\ngit --no-pager diff --check; cat /tmp/pay381-replay.log; node -e 'const fs=require(\"fs\");console.log(\"Seconds since replay:\",Math.round(Date.now()/1000-JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(\"data/replay_state.json\")).last_run_at))'\n"]
[143.578355, "o", "cat >> README.md <<'EOF'\r\n"]
[143.582576, "o", "\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> ## PAY-381 operations\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> Webhook deliveries always require a valid `Paygate-Signature`, including retries.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> Replay-token headers do not bypass verification. Signature checks use the raw request\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> bytes, the configured active secrets, and the configured timestamp tolerance. Event\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> IDs are persisted so successful deliveries are not processed or audited again.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> For trusted outage payloads already in `ops/backlog/`, use `npm run replay-backlog`.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> It skips processed event IDs and uses the same refund policy as the receiver. Keep\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> payments on-call's refund-storm guard intact: at most 20 events per run, with at least\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> 120 seconds between runs. Repeat after each interval until the command reports zero\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> remaining events. This local recovery path does not require weakening HTTP signature\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> verification or changing internal API permissions.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> The approved policy auto-approves INR refunds up to and including ₹5,000 (500000\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[143.582756, "o", "minor units); larger refunds and all other currencies go to manual review."]
[143.583821, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> EOF\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
